  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 8 fixes on needs-wording (audit of fbaa84d: 1 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM), with the owner's decisions of 2026-11-16 and the teacher-reviewer's General Chemistry symptoms. HIGH-1: exportNeeds hands a digest entry clustering several findings of a kind with choices (DIGEST_CHOICES or the wording's) in as one question per finding (key#finding id, its own passage, choices and basis; splitEntry), so each can be settled from Alembic; a kind no choice acts on stays one question in words. buildDigest, rootCause, bases and answerDigest are unchanged. MEDIUM-2: a digest question id hashes the entry's bases; exportNeeds refuses a changeset id the needs record already holds. Owner (b), one click: a question whose choices are all of Apply the suggestion / Change it differently / Keep it / Drop it / Later, of a kind without Coursewerk's own choices and not binding, takes words optional; the choice is recorded as the instructor's words. Confirm, Keep as written, Keep on an edit, Accept as mine, Still correct keep words required. Change it differently without words is skipped, marked once (asked again). Owner (a): the choice reads Apply the suggestion (unchanged). Wording: a passage a finding names that the text no longer holds is said so and offers no choice; a cluster names at most five chapters; a harness note naming its own place says it once (typographic apostrophes compared). Tests: audit8 probes adopted (tests/needs-wording.audit8.test.mjs); audit7 HIGH-1 and MEDIUM-7 adapted (the cluster is now split; the legacy cluster record is built by asCluster and still reads a choice as words); audit MEDIUM-4 expects words optional; two new wording tests (one click; the reviewer's symptoms). Full suite under lockf, 2 workers: 1271 tests, 1268 passed; the 3 failures were the two audit7 tests (before their adaptation; 7/7 pass after) and system-index (the index was stale until regenerated here).",
